{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","title":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1886,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:oriented-unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:two-unit-normals]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:basis-realizing-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","line":3065,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[An Orientation Selects a Unit Normal]\n\\label{prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal}\n\n\\uses{def:oriented-unit-normal, lem:two-unit-normals, lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span, lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal, lem:basis-realizing-orientation, lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos, def:unit-normal, def:metric-preserving}\n\n\n\n\nIf $n\\ge1$ and $o$ is a pointwise orientation of an isometrically immersed hypersurface, exactly one unit normal at each $x$ induces $o(x)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:two-unit-normals,lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span,lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal,lem:basis-realizing-orientation,lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos}\n\\sketch The normal space is spanned by a unit $w_0$ and its only unit normals are $\\pm w_0$. Evaluate the contracted form of $w_0$ on an $o(x)$-positive basis; the value is nonzero, and exactly one of it and its negative is positive.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[An Orientation Selects a Unit Normal] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a657869737473756e697175652d6f7269656e7465642d756e69742d6e6f726d616c\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aoriented-unit-normal\">↗ def:oriented-unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atwo-unit-normals\">↗ lem:two-unit-normals</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apointwise-unit-normal-span\">↗ lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-neg-normal\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abasis-realizing-orientation\">↗ lem:basis-realizing-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aoriented-unit-normal-iff-pos\">↗ lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal\">↗ def:unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n\\ge 1$\">$n\\ge 1$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o$\">$o$</span> is a pointwise orientation of an isometrically immersed hypersurface, exactly one unit normal at each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> induces <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o(x)$\">$o(x)$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atwo-unit-normals\">↗ lem:two-unit-normals</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apointwise-unit-normal-span\">↗ lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-neg-normal\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abasis-realizing-orientation\">↗ lem:basis-realizing-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aoriented-unit-normal-iff-pos\">↗ lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos</a> \\sketch The normal space is spanned by a unit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w_0$\">$w_0$</span> and its only unit normals are <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pm w_0$\">$\\pm w_0$</span>. Evaluate the contracted form of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w_0$\">$w_0$</span> on an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o(x)$\">$o(x)$</span>-positive basis; the value is nonzero, and exactly one of it and its negative is positive. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>"